<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Statue of Ebih-Il</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2400 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/25th-century-bce">25th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The statue of Ebih-Il is an alabaster figure of a seated worshipper from the temple of Ishtar at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a>, made around 2400 BCE. It shows Ebih-Il, a superintendent of Mari, wearing a sheepskin skirt, with inlaid eyes of shell and lapis lazuli. Found by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andre-parrot">André Parrot</a>'s team in the 1930s, it is now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a> and is a masterpiece of early Mesopotamian sculpture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/statue-of-ebih-il.jpg" alt="Statue of Ebih-Il" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Applejuice · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ebih-ii_en_priere.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
